Now, when you click on an album detail item, it should navigate to the `songDetail` composable and start playing the 30-second preview of the song.

If you don't want a separate UI for the song detail screen and want to play the preview directly in the album detail screen, you can modify the `AlbumDetailItem` composable and the `playPreview` function. Here are the steps:

1. Remove the navigation to the songDetail screen in `AlbumDetailItem` onClick:

```kotlin
.clickable(onClick = {
    playPreview(context, song.preview)
})
```

2. Add a `DisposableEffect` in the `AlbumDetailItem` composable to stop and release the player when the composable is disposed. You will also need to create and store the player as a `rememberSaveable` state variable:

```kotlin
@Composable
fun AlbumDetailItem(song: Song, navController: NavController) {
    val context = LocalContext.current

    val (player, setPlayer) = rememberSaveable { mutableStateOf<SimpleExoPlayer?>(null) }

    DisposableEffect(Unit) {
        onDispose {
            player?.stop()
            player?.release()
        }
    }

    // ...
}
```

3. Update the `playPreview` function to accept a lambda function that sets the player in the state variable and remove the `player.release()` call:

```kotlin
private fun playPreview(context: Context, previewUrl: String, onPlayerCreated: (SimpleExoPlayer) -> Unit) {
    val player = SimpleExoPlayer.Builder(context).build()
    val mediaItem = MediaItem.fromUri(previewUrl)
    player.setMediaItem(mediaItem)
    player.prepare()
    player.playWhenReady = true
    onPlayerCreated(player)

    // Stop playing after 30 seconds
    player.seekTo(30000)
    player.addListener(object : Player.Listener {
        override fun onPositionDiscontinuity(
            oldPosition: Player.PositionInfo,
            newPosition: Player.PositionInfo,
            reason: Int
        ) {
            if (newPosition.windowIndex != oldPosition.windowIndex) {
                player.stop()
            }
        }
    })
}
```

4. Update the `playPreview` function call in the `onClick` lambda function: 

```kotlin
.clickable(onClick = {
    playPreview(context, song.preview, onPlayerCreated = { createdPlayer ->
        setPlayer(createdPlayer)
    })
})
```

In this updated version, clicking an `AlbumDetailItem` will play the preview without navigating to another screen. The preview playback will be stopped and the player resources will be released when the composable is disposed (e.g., when navigating away from the album detail screen).

