Here's the modified version of the script with currency conversion from USD to IDR using real-time exchange rates:

```php
<?php

function get_exchange_rate($base_currency, $target_currency) {
    $url = "https://api.exchangerate-api.com/v4/latest/{$base_currency}";
    $response = wp_remote_get($url);
    if (is_wp_error($response)) {
        return false;
    }

    $exchange_data = json_decode(wp_remote_retrieve_body($response), true);
    if (!isset($exchange_data['rates'][$target_currency])) {
        return false;
    }

    return $exchange_data['rates'][$target_currency];
}

function cmdcp_postback_api($data)
{
    global $wpdb;
    $wp_prefix = $wpdb->prefix;

    $data['merchant_transaction_id'] = trim($data['merchant_transaction_id']);
    $data['transaction_amount'] = trim($data['transaction_amount']);
    $data['commission_amount'] = trim($data['commission_amount']);
    $data['transaction_status'] = trim($data['transaction_status']);
    $data['click_id'] = trim($data['click_id']);
    $data['transaction_date'] = trim($data['transaction_date']);

    // Get the exchange rate
    $usd_to_idr_rate = get_exchange_rate('USD', 'IDR');
    if (!$usd_to_idr_rate) {
        $usd_to_idr_rate = 1; // default to 1 if API call fails
    }

    // Convert amounts to IDR
    $data['transaction_amount'] = $data['transaction_amount'] * $usd_to_idr_rate;
    $data['commission_amount'] = $data['commission_amount'] * $usd_to_idr_rate;

    // Rest of the code remains the same
    // ...
}
```

The function `get_exchange_rate($base_currency, $target_currency)` retrieves the current exchange rates using the Exchange Rate API. The script then converts the transaction_amount and commission_amount into IDR based on the real-time exchange rate. If the API call fails, the rate is set to 1 by default.

Please note that you might need to adjust the script according to your requirements.

