To create a React Native Expo page to capture a 45-second video of yourself, follow the steps below:

1. Install `expo-camera` and `expo-permissions` packages, as well as `expo-video-thumbnails`.

```bash
expo install expo-camera
expo install expo-permissions
expo install expo-video-thumbnails
```

2. Import necessary components and hooks.

```javascript
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { View, Text, StyleSheet, TouchableOpacity, Image } from 'react-native';
import { Camera } from 'expo-camera';
import * as Permissions from 'expo-permissions';
import { createThumbnail } from 'expo-video-thumbnails';
```

3. Set up the app component for recording the video.

```javascript
export default function App() {
  const [hasCameraPermission, setHasCameraPermission] = useState(null);
  const [isRecording, setIsRecording] = useState(false);
  const [cameraRef, setCameraRef] = useState(null);
  const [videoUri, setVideoUri] = useState(null);
  const [thumbnailUri, setThumbnailUri] = useState(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    getPermissions();
  }, []);

  const getPermissions = async () => {
    const { status } = await Permissions.askAsync(Permissions.CAMERA);
    setHasCameraPermission(status === 'granted');
  };

  const startRecording = async () => {
    setIsRecording(true);
    const videoRec = await cameraRef.recordAsync({ maxDuration: 45 });
    setVideoUri(videoRec.uri);
  };

  const stopRecording = async () => {
    setIsRecording(false);
    cameraRef.stopRecording();
    const {uri} = await createThumbnail({source: videoUri});
    setThumbnailUri(uri);
  };
```

4. Implement UI components with start, stop, retake, and save buttons.

```javascript
