This error usually occurs when you are trying to access the `$options` property of an undefined or null object. It means that the object you are trying to access does not exist or has not been initialized.

To resolve the issue, you need to make sure that the object you are trying to access is defined and initialized properly. You can also use conditional statements or null check to avoid accessing properties on undefined objects. 

For example, if you are trying to access the `$options` property of an object named `vm` in Vue.js, you can use the following code to avoid the error:

```
if (vm && vm.$options) {
  // Access vm.$options safely
}
```

This code checks if the `vm` object is defined and then checks if it has the `$options` property before accessing it.

