Comparing two .docx files with images and text is quite complex. One of the most popular libraries for working with .docx files in Java is Apache POI. Here's an example of how to compare two .docx files using Apache POI:

1. Add dependencies for `poi-ooxml` and `poi-scratchpad`.

```xml
<dependencies>
  <dependency>
    <groupId>org.apache.poi</groupId>
    <artifactId>poi-ooxml</artifactId>
    <version>5.2.0</version>
  </dependency>
  <dependency>
    <groupId>org.apache.poi</groupId>
    <artifactId>poi-scratchpad</artifactId>
    <version>5.2.0</version>
  </dependency>
</dependencies>
```

2. Now we can start writing the code to compare two .docx files.

```java
import org.apache.poi.xwpf.usermodel.*;
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import java.util.Objects;

public class WordComparison {

    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {
        String filePath1 = "path/to/your/document1.docx";
        String filePath2 = "path/to/your/document2.docx";

        FileInputStream fis1 = new FileInputStream(filePath1);
        FileInputStream fis2 = new FileInputStream(filePath2);

        XWPFDocument doc1 = new XWPFDocument(fis1);
        XWPFDocument doc2 = new XWPFDocument(fis2);

        boolean areEqual = compareDocuments(doc1, doc2);
        System.out.println("Documents are " + (areEqual ? "equal" : "not equal"));

        fis1.close();
        fis2.close();
    }

    public static boolean compareDocuments(XWPFDocument doc1, XWPFDocument doc2) {
        if (doc1.getNumberOfPages() != doc2.getNumberOfPages()) {
            return false;
        }

        // Compare paragraphs
        if (doc1.getParagraphs().size() != doc2.getParagraphs().size()) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < doc1.getParagraphs().size(); i++) {
            XWPFParagraph p1 = doc1.getParagraphs().get(i);
            XWPFParagraph p2 = doc2.getParagraphs().get(i);
            if (!Objects.equals(p1.getText(), p2.getText())) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        // Compare images
        if (doc1.getAllPictures().size() != doc2.getAllPictures().size()) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < doc1.getAllPictures().size(); i++) {
            XWPFPictureData pic1 = doc1.getAllPictures().get(i);
            XWPFPictureData pic2 = doc2.getAllPictures().get(i);
            if (!Objects.equals(pic1.getFileName(), pic2.getFileName())) {
                return false;
            }

            byte[] pic1Content = pic1.getData();
            byte[] pic2Content = pic2.getData();
            if (!compareByteArrays(pic1Content, pic2Content)) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    public static boolean compareByteArrays(byte[] array1, byte[] array2) {
        if (array1 == array2) {
            return true;
        }

        if (array1.length != array2.length) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < array1.length; i++) {
            if (array1[i] != array2[i]) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }
}
```

Run the `WordComparison` class by setting the `filePath1` and `filePath2` variables to your target .docx files. This example will compare the text paragraphs and images but not their positions in the documents. If the documents have identical text and images but in a different order, they will be considered equal by this comparison. If you wish to perform more advanced comparisons, you'll need to adapt the code accordingly.

