You can use the QPainter class in conjunction with QPixmap to draw the source QPixmap onto the destination QPixmap at the specified location. Here's an example function that demonstrates how to copy a QPixmap image to another QPixmap image at a specific location:

```cpp
#include <QPixmap>
#include <QPainter>

void copyPixmapAtLocation(QPixmap &dst, const QPixmap &src, int x, int y)
{
    QPainter painter(&dst);        // Start painting on the destination QPixmap
    painter.drawPixmap(x, y, src); // Draw the source QPixmap at the specified location (x, y)
    painter.end();                 // End painting
}
```

