```javascript
function lerp(a, b, t, d) {
  return a * (1 - t / d) + b * t / d;
}
```

You can now pass a dampening factor when calling the lerp function. For example:

```javascript
this.vxForce = lerp(this.maxVx, this.minVx, (wave + 8) / 432, 5); // where 5 is the dampening factor
```

