To create a table with editable cells, dynamically add rows, remove rows, and custom cell configuration using JavaScript, follow the steps below:

1. First, create a basic HTML structure with a table element and necessary controls like buttons for adding and removing rows.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Editable Table</title>
</head>
<body>
    <button onclick="addRow()">Add Row</button>
    <button onclick="removeRow()">Remove Row</button>

    <table id="myTable" border="1">
        <tbody>
            <!-- Table rows will be added dynamically -->
        </tbody>
    </table>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

2. Now, create a script.js file and write the following JavaScript code in it:

```javascript
// Function to make a table cell editable
function makeCellEditable(cell) {
    cell.onclick = function () {
        const input = document.createElement('input');
        input.setAttribute('type', 'text');
        input.value = this.innerHTML;

        input.onblur = function () {
            cell.innerHTML = this.value;
            makeCellEditable(cell);
        };

        this.innerHTML = '';
        this.appendChild(input);
        input.focus();
    };
}

// Function to add a table row
function addRow() {
    const table = document.getElementById('myTable');
    const row = table.insertRow(-1);

    // Adding three cells to the row
    for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
        const cell = row.insertCell(i);
        cell.innerHTML = 'Editable Cell';

        // Custom cell configuration
        cell.style.backgroundColor = i === 0 ? 'green' : (i === 1 ? 'blue' : 'red');

        makeCellEditable(cell);
    }
}

// Function to remove a table row
function removeRow() {
    const table = document.getElementById('myTable');
    const rowCount = table.rows.length;

    if (rowCount > 0) {
        table.deleteRow(rowCount - 1);
    }
}
```

This code creates a simple editable table with dynamic add and remove row functionality. Each cell has its own configuration, like a different background color. You can customize this code further according to your additional requirements.

You can use `createElement` to create `select` and `option` elements and add them to your table cells. Here's an example:

