Implement a load balancer to your Kubernetes cluster to distribute requests between your running instances. There are various load balancers available, e.g., NGINX, HAProxy, or you can use a cloud provider's load balancer. This will help distribute OkHttp requests evenly among your available instances.

2. Use Connection Pooling:

OkHttp uses connection pooling to improve performance. By default, OkHttp allows up to 5 idle connections per host. You can configure the ConnectionPool settings to manage idle connections and keep-alive duration as needed. This will improve your request distribution in your cluster:

