To print an integer in binary format, we need to convert it to binary first and then print it. The following code snippet can be used to print an integer in binary format using `printf`: 

```c
void printBinary(int num){
    int binaryNum[32];
    int i = 0;
    while(num > 0){
        binaryNum[i] = num % 2;
        num = num / 2;
        i++;
    }
    for(int j=i-1; j>=0; j--){
        printf("%d", binaryNum[j]);
    }
}
```

This function takes an integer as input and converts it to binary format using the modulo-2 division method. It then prints the binary digits in reverse order. 

