The issue is in your `Terrain.cpp` destructor. You commented out the cleanup calls for `terrainMesh` and `terrainMaterial`. Since they are not being cleaned up in `Terrain`, a double free occurs when the `Mesh` and `Material` destructors are called during the `GameObject` destruction in `Scene::Shutdown`.

To fix this issue, you can uncomment the cleanup calls in the `Terrain` destructor:

```cpp
Terrain::~Terrain() {
    // Cleanup any resources associated with the Terrain class
    terrainMesh.Cleanup();
    terrainMaterial.Cleanup();
}
```

Alternatively, you can manage the resources of `Mesh` and `Material` using smart pointers like `std::shared_ptr` to avoid double frees and manage the resources automatically. You can consider converting the member variables `terrainMesh` and `terrainMaterial` in `Terrain` class to `std::shared_ptr<Mesh>` and `std::shared_ptr<Material>`, and then initializing them using `std::make_shared<Mesh>()` and `std::make_shared<Material>()`. This way, you don't have to worry about freeing resources in the Terrain destructor manually.

