However, there might be cases where you attempt to clean up resources that have not been entirely initialized. To avoid this, add an additional flag to your Pipeline class to track its initialization state and use it within the Cleanup() function to make sure you attempt to clean up only if the resource is initialized.

Modify your Pipeline class to include a `bool initialized` member variable, set its default value to `false` in the constructor, and set it to `true` once the CreateGraphicsPipeline() function is successfully executed.

