To use the WolfLive.Api to send messages in a specific group, you need to follow these steps:

1. Clone the repository:
```
git clone https://github.com/calico-crusade/WolfLive.Api.git
```

2. Make sure you have installed .NET Core SDK to build and run the project: https://dotnet.microsoft.com/download

3. Navigate to the folder that contains the solution file (.sln) and execute the following command:
```
dotnet build
```

4. Add the following code to the sample or your own application:

```csharp
using System;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using WolfLive.Api;

namespace WolfLive.Sample
{
    class Program
    {
        static async Task Main(string[] args)
        {
            var email = "your_email@example.com";
            var password = "your_password";
            var groupId = "your_group_id";

            var api = new WolfApi("wss://v2-188.web.wolf.live");

            // Connects and logs in
            Console.WriteLine("Connecting...");
            await api.Connect();
            Console.WriteLine("Connected! Logging in...");
            var me = await api.Login(email, password); // use the credentials provided
            Console.WriteLine("Logged in as: " + me.Nickname);

            // Send a message to the specific group
            await api.SendMessage(groupId, "This is a test message!");

            // Subscribe to the message event in the group
            api.OnMessage += (sender, message) =>
            {
                Console.WriteLine($"Received message from {message.Sender.Nickname}: {message.Content}");
            };

            // Keep the application running
            await Task.Delay(-1);
        }
    }
}
```
Make sure to replace `"your_email@example.com"`, `"your_password"` and `"your_group_id"` with your Wolf credentials and the target group ID, respectively.

5. Run the sample application:
```
dotnet run --project path/to/your/Application.csproj
```

Now, the application should connect, log in, and send a message to the specified group using the WolfLive.Api.

Unfortunately, WolfLive.Api does not natively support Google authentication out-of-the-box. However, you can work around this by obtaining the Bearer token (also known as the Access token) yourself upon logging in to your Google account and then using it with the API.

Here are the steps to do this:

1. Obtain your Bearer token by following Google's OAuth 2.0 guide: https://developers.google.com/identity/protocols/oauth2

The Google OAuth 2.0 document contains details on setting up the required Google APIs, creating client secrets, getting authorization codes, and exchanging them for access tokens.

2. Once you have your Bearer token, modify the WolfLive.Api code to use the token instead of `Email` and `Password`. Specifically, change the `ApiSession.cs` file in the `User` method, around line 100.

Replace this code:

```csharp
_data.Add("email", email);
_data.Add("password", password);
```

with this:

```csharp
_data.Add("accessToken", bearer_token);
_data.Add("app", "google");
```

Make sure to replace `bearer_token` with your obtained Bearer token.

3. Modify the sample application to remove the email and password arguments, and instead pass the Bearer token directly, like:

```csharp
