To refer to `datacode.rs` from `lib.rs` in the `subproject`, you can use a relative path to reach the file. 
Assuming that `lib.rs` is at `project/subproject/src/lib.rs`, you can use `super::..` to reach the top-level `src` directory of `project` and then navigate to `datacode.rs`. 

Here's an example:

```rust
// project/subproject/src/lib.rs

mod some_module {

    use super::super::datacode::MyGlobalStruct;

    // Use MyGlobalStruct here

}
```

The `use` statement above starts at `lib.rs` (which is in `project/subproject/src/`), moves up one directory to `project/subproject/`, then moves up another directory to `project/src/`, and finally navigates to `project/src/datacode.rs` to import `MyGlobalStruct` into the module. 

Note that the `super` keyword represents the parent directory of the current file (or module). In this case, it moves up two directories to reach the top-level `src` directory of `project`.

To add `datacode.rs` as a dependency in the `subproject`'s `Cargo.toml` file, you can use a relative path that starts at the root of the project, which is the same as `../` from the `subproject` directory. 

Here's an example `Cargo.toml` file for `subproject` with the dependency on `datacode.rs`:

```toml
[package]
name = "my_subproject"
version = "0.1.0"
authors = ["Your Name <you@example.com>"]
edition = "2018"

[dependencies]
my_datacode = { path = "../src" }
```

The `path` key specifies a path to the source directory for the dependency, which in this case is `../src`. This will allow `lib.rs` and `main.rs` in the `subproject` to access the `MyGlobalStruct` defined in `datacode.rs`. 

To use `MyGlobalStruct` in `lib.rs` or `main.rs` of the `subproject`, you can import it like this:

```rust
use my_datacode::MyGlobalStruct;

// Now you can use MyGlobalStruct however you like
``` 

Note that `datacode.rs` needs to have a `pub` declaration for `MyGlobalStruct` and be wrapped in a module for it to be visible outside of its own module. For example, `datacode.rs` could look like this:

```rust
pub mod datacode {
    pub struct MyGlobalStruct {
        // ...
    }

    // Other code for datacode module
}
```

And you would import it with this code in `lib.rs` or `main.rs`:

```rust
use my_datacode::datacode::MyGlobalStruct;

// Now you can use MyGlobalStruct however you like
```

