Creating an interactive map with nodes and popout windows in a React app can be achieved using Mapbox or Leaflet libraries, along with their respective React bindings: react-mapbox-gl for Mapbox and react-leaflet for Leaflet.

I will provide an outline to implement this using both react-mapbox-gl and react-leaflet. Just pick the one you prefer.

**Solution using react-mapbox-gl**

1. Install the required dependencies:

```
npm install --save react-mapbox-gl mapbox-gl
```

2. Set up the Mapbox Access Token from the Mapbox account in your project's `.env` file:

```
REACT_APP_MAPBOX_TOKEN="<your_mapbox_access_token>"
```

3. Create your map component using react-mapbox-gl:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import ReactMapboxGl, { Marker, Popup } from 'react-mapbox-gl';

const MapboxAccessToken = process.env.REACT_APP_MAPBOX_TOKEN;

const Map = ReactMapboxGl({
  accessToken: MapboxAccessToken,
});

const CustomMap = ({ nodes }) => {
  return (
    <Map
      style="mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v11"
      containerStyle={{
        height: '100vh',
        width: '100vw',
      }}
    >
      {nodes.map((node, index) => (
        <>
          <Marker coordinates={[node.longitude, node.latitude]}>
            <div className="marker" />
          </Marker>
          <Popup coordinates={[node.longitude, node.latitude]} closeButton={false}>
            <div>
              {node.previewData}
              <br />
              <a href={node.detailedDataUrl}>Detailed Data Page</a>
            </div>
          </Popup>
        </>
      ))}
    </Map>
  );
};

export default CustomMap;
```

**Solution using react-leaflet**

1. Install the required dependencies:

```
npm install --save leaflet react-leaflet
```

2. Install `@types/leaflet` if you are using TypeScript:

```
npm install --save @types/leaflet
```

3. Import stylesheets for Leaflet:

```javascript
// In your index.js or index.css
import 'leaflet/dist/leaflet.css';
```

4. Create your map component using react-leaflet:

```javascript
import React from 'react';
import { MapContainer, TileLayer, Marker, Popup } from 'react-leaflet';

const CustomMap = ({ nodes }) => {
  return (
    <MapContainer center={[50, 10]} zoom={4} style={{ height: '100vh', width: '100vw' }}>
      <TileLayer
        attribution='&copy; <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright">OpenStreetMap</a> contributors'
        url="https://{s}.tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png"
      />
      {nodes.map((node, index) => (
        <Marker position={[node.latitude, node.longitude]} key={index}>
          <Popup>
            {node.previewData}
            <br />
            <a href={node.detailedDataUrl}>Detailed Data Page</a>
          </Popup>
        </Marker>
      ))}
    </MapContainer>
  );
};

export default CustomMap;
```

In both examples, you will need to pass a `nodes` prop to the `CustomMap` component which contains an array of objects with `latitude`, `longitude`, `previewData`, and `detailedDataUrl` properties.

For custom marker and popup styles, refer to the respective libraries' documentation.

