Here are the basic steps you need to follow to create the circuit and write the code for Arduino:

1. Connect the variable signal source to an analog input pin of Arduino through the ADC. This will allow you to read the analog signal values.

2. Use a comparator or level shifter to convert the analog input signal into a digital signal (logic high or low) as per the given criteria.

3. Connect the output of the comparator to a digital input pin of Arduino. This digital input will be used to determine whether the lamp should be turned on or off.

4. Connect the gate of the MOSFET (or the base of the transistor) to a digital output pin of Arduino. This will allow Arduino to control the current flowing through the lamp.

