To convert the LocalDateTime object to a long timestamp, we first convert it to a ZoneDateTime object using the atZone() method with the system default time zone. Finally, we convert this ZonedDateTime object to an Instant object using the toInstant() method and get the Epoch timestamp in milliseconds using the toEpochMilli() method.

