To prevent Bootstrap SCSS from being compiled every time you run `yarn run dev-server`, you can configure Webpack to output the compiled CSS from Bootstrap to a separate CSS file. Then, you can include that file in your HTML without having to compile it during development.

Here are the steps to do this:

1. Install `mini-css-extract-plugin` to generate the separate CSS file:

```bash
yarn add -D mini-css-extract-plugin
```

2. In your `webpack.config.js`, import the `MiniCssExtractPlugin` and configure it alongside the SCSS loader:

```javascript
// webpack.config.js
const MiniCssExtractPlugin = require('mini-css-extract-plugin');

// Other Webpack configurations...

module.exports = {
  // Other configurations...

  module: {
    rules: [
      // Other rules...

      // SCSS Loader
      {
        test: /\.scss$/,
        use: [
          process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production'
            ? MiniCssExtractPlugin.loader
            : 'style-loader',
          'css-loader',
          'sass-loader',
        ],
      },
    ],
  },

  plugins: [
    // Other plugins...

    // Add the MiniCssExtractPlugin for production builds
    ...(process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' ? [new MiniCssExtractPlugin()] : []),
  ],
};
```

3. Create a new SCSS file, for example, `bootstrap.scss`, and import Bootstrap SCSS:

```scss
// bootstrap.scss
@import '~bootstrap/scss/bootstrap';
```

4. Instead of importing the `bootstrap.scss` file in your JavaScript entry point, compile it to a separate CSS file:

```bash
# Run this command in production mode:
yarn run encore production

# This will generate the compiled Bootstrap CSS file in the 'public/build' folder
```

5. Include the compiled CSS file in your HTML:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <!-- Other metadata -->

    <!-- Include the compiled Bootstrap CSS -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/build/bootstrap.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <!-- Your app markup -->

    <!-- Include your app's JavaScript bundle -->
    <script src="/build/app.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
```

Now, when you run `yarn run dev-server`, it won't compile the Bootstrap SCSS every time. The compiled CSS file will be loaded separately from your HTML file.

Note that you'll need to run `yarn run encore production` whenever you make changes to the Bootstrap SCSS to update the compiled CSS file.

