Here's how to configure caching for `sass-loader` in your `webpack.config.js` file:

1. In your existing rule for SCSS Loader, extend the 'sass-loader' configuration with the 'options' property containing 'implementation' and 'sassOptions' for caching purposes.

```javascript
// webpack.config.js

const path = require("path");
const sass = require("sass");

// Other Webpack configurations...

module.exports = {
  // Other configurations...

  module: {
    rules: [
      // Other rules...

      // SCSS Loader
      {
        test: /\.scss$/,
        use: [
          "style-loader",
          "css-loader",
          {
            loader: "sass-loader",
            options: {
              implementation: sass,
              sassOptions: {
                includePaths: [path.resolve(__dirname, "node_modules")],
                cache: path.resolve(__dirname, "node_modules/.sass-cache"),
              },
            },
          },
        ],
      },
    ],
  },

  // Other configurations...
};
```

This configuration will cache the output of `sass-loader`, so Bootstrap SCSS won't be compiled every time you run `yarn run dev-server` as long as the SCSS files haven't changed. This will speed up your builds significantly.

You can continue to import Bootstrap SCSS in your `app.js` like this:

```javascript
// app.js
import "~bootstrap/scss/bootstrap";
// Other imports and code
```

