Yes, you can prevent the compilation of Bootstrap SCSS by including the compiled CSS file instead of the SCSS version. To do this, follow these steps:

1. Install Bootstrap CSS package if you haven't already:

```
yarn add bootstrap
```

2. Remove the import for the Bootstrap SCSS file in your project's entry SCSS or JS file:

```scss
// Remove this line
@import '~bootstrap/scss/bootstrap';
```

```js
// Or remove this line in your JS file
import 'bootstrap/scss/bootstrap.scss';
```

3. Import the compiled Bootstrap CSS file in your project's entry JS file:

```js
import 'bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css';
```

This way, you will use the pre-built Bootstrap CSS, skipping the SCSS compilation in your development environment. Keep in mind that this method won't allow you to customize Bootstrap variables or use its mixins. To make changes or use mixins, you'll need to override styles in your custom SCSS file after importing the pre-built CSS.

