A context menu is a floating menu that appears when the user performs a long press on an item in the user interface (such as a button or a list view item). The context menu typically contains a set of actions that can be performed on the selected item.

In Android, you can create a context menu by following these steps:

1. Define the menu item layout in an XML file. For example, create a file named `context_menu.xml` in the `res/menu` directory, and add the following items:

```xml
<menu xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:id="@+id/context_menu_item1"
        android:icon="@drawable/icon1"
        android:title="Item 1" />
    <item android:id="@+id/context_menu_item2"
        android:icon="@drawable/icon2"
        android:title="Item 2" />
    <item android:id="@+id/context_menu_item3"
        android:icon="@drawable/icon3"
        android:title="Item 3" />
</menu>
```

2. Register the view to which you want to attach the context menu for long presses in the `onCreate()` method of your activity or fragment. For example, if you want to attach the context menu to a button, you can do the following:

```kotlin
val myButton = findViewById<Button>(R.id.my_button)
registerForContextMenu(myButton)
```

The `registerForContextMenu()` method is called with the view that you want to associate with the context menu.

3. Override the `onCreateContextMenu()` method in your activity or fragment. Here, you specify how to inflate the context menu layout and define the actions to take when a menu item is selected:

```kotlin
override fun onCreateContextMenu(menu: ContextMenu?, v: View?,
        menuInfo: ContextMenu.ContextMenuInfo?) {
    super.onCreateContextMenu(menu, v, menuInfo)
    menuInflater.inflate(R.menu.context_menu, menu)
}

override fun onContextItemSelected(item: MenuItem): Boolean {
    when (item.itemId) {
        R.id.context_menu_item1 -> {
            // Perform action 1
            return true
        }
        R.id.context_menu_item2 -> {
            // Perform action 2
            return true
        }
        R.id.context_menu_item3 -> {
            // Perform action 3
            return true
        }
        else -> return super.onContextItemSelected(item)
    }
}
```

Here, `onCreateContextMenu()` inflates the context menu layout from the XML file and binds it to the menu parameter. You can customize the layout and menu items as needed.

The `onContextItemSelected()` function is called when a context menu item is selected. You can identify the selected item by checking its ID, and then perform the appropriate action.

That's it! When the user long-presses the associated view, the context menu will appear, and the selected item's action will be executed when the user taps it.

Pseudocode:

1. Initialize LED pins and start/stop button pin.
2. Set Timer 0 for desired delay.
3. Set initial state of LEDs - First group on (0, 1, 2, 3) and second group off (4, 5, 6, 7).
4. Loop forever:
    a. If Start/Stop button is pressed:
        i. Toggle flashing state (if LEDs are flashing, stop them, if not, start flashing)
        ii. Debounce the button to avoid multiple triggers.
    b. If flashing state is enabled:
        i. Toggle the LEDs (swap their On/Off states)
        ii. Delay using Timer 0.

C-code:

```c
#include "driver/gpio.h"
#include "freertos/FreeRTOS.h"
#include "freertos/task.h"

#define BUTTON_GPIO GPIO_NUM_13
#define DELAY 500 / portTICK_PERIOD_MS

void setup() {
  gpio_pad_select_gpio(BUTTON_GPIO);
  gpio_set_direction(BUTTON_GPIO, GPIO_MODE_INPUT);

  for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    gpio_pad_select_gpio(i);
    gpio_set_direction(i, GPIO_MODE_OUTPUT);
  }

  // Set initial state of LEDs
  for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {
    gpio_set_level(i, 1);
  }
  for (int i = 4; i < 8; i++) {
    gpio_set_level(i, 0);
  }
}

void toggleLEDs() {
  for (int i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
    int level = gpio_get_level(i);
    gpio_set_level(i, !level);
  }
}

void loop() {
  static bool flashEnabled = false;
  static uint32_t lastButtonPress = 0;

  uint32_t now = xTaskGetTickCount();

  // Start/Stop button is pressed
  if (gpio_get_level(BUTTON_GPIO) == 1 && (now - lastButtonPress) > 100) {
    // Toggle flashing state
    flashEnabled = !flashEnabled;
    lastButtonPress = now;

    // Debounce button
    vTaskDelay(50 / portTICK_PERIOD_MS);
  }

  if (flashEnabled) {
    toggleLEDs();
    vTaskDelay(DELAY);
  }
}

void app_main() {
  setup();
  while (1) {
    loop();
  }
}
```

