If I understand your issue correctly, you have two LineSeries in your chart, each with different yAxis, and the zooming doesn't work as expected for both of them. The solution to this problem is to ensure each yAxis is zoomed separately for each LineSeries during the zoom event.

Here's an updated version of your `mouseScrolled` method which considers multiple yAxis:

```java
@Override
public void mouseScrolled(MouseEvent event) {
    if ((event.stateMask & SWT.CTRL) == SWT.CTRL) {
        if (event.count > 0) {
            if (zoomXCentred && zoomYCentred) {
                chart.getAxisSet().zoomIn();
            } else {
                Rectangle bounds = chart.getPlotArea().getBounds();

                // Zooming in both X and Y axes
                if (zoomXCentred) {
                    for (IAxis axis : chart.getAxisSet().getXAxes()) {
                        axis.zoomIn();
                    }
                } else {
                    zoomAxisAtMousePosition(event, bounds, true);
                }

                if (zoomYCentred) {
                    for (IAxis axis : chart.getAxisSet().getYAxes()) {
                        axis.zoomIn();
                    }
                } else {
                    zoomAxisAtMousePosition(event, bounds, false);
                }
            }
        } else if (event.count < 0) {
            chart.getAxisSet().zoomOut();
        }

        chart.redraw();
    }
}

private void zoomAxisAtMousePosition(MouseEvent event, Rectangle bounds, boolean isXAxis) {
    int axisIndex = 0;
    // Loop through all relevant axes
    for (IAxis axis : isXAxis ? chart.getAxisSet().getXAxes() : chart.getAxisSet().getYAxes()) {
        Range chartRange = axis.getRange();

        // Calculate the real position of the mouse on the axis
        int eventPos = isXAxis ? event.x : event.y;
        int axisLength = isXAxis ? bounds.width : bounds.height;
        double realPos;

        if (isXAxis) {
            realPos = chartRange.lower + ((chartRange.upper - chartRange.lower) * ((double) eventPos / axisLength));
        } else {
            realPos = chartRange.upper - ((chartRange.upper - chartRange.lower) * ((double) eventPos / axisLength));
        }

        axis.zoomIn(realPos);

        // Check if we zoomed on top of the other curve and return to the default range if needed
        Range updatedRange = axis.getRange();
        for (ISeries series : chart.getSeriesSet().getSeries()) {
            if (isXAxis && series.getYAxisId() == axisIndex || !isXAxis && series.getXAxisId() == axisIndex) {
                double[] lineSeriesData = isXAxis ? series.getYSeries() : series.getXSeries();
                double maxValue = Arrays.stream(lineSeriesData).max().orElse(Double.MIN_VALUE);

                if (updatedRange.upper < maxValue) {
                    axis.setRange(chartRange);
                }
            }
        }
        axisIndex++;
    }
}
```

Now, the updated `mouseScrolled` method considers multiple yAxis, zooms them separately, and checks if the zoomed axis isn't going on top of the other curve. If it does, it returns to the default range to avoid overlapping.

