Here's an example of a Neo4j Java application for a time-varying graph with parameterizable schema, varying properties in relationships, and sharding for distributed processing:

```java
import org.neo4j.driver.*;

import java.time.LocalDateTime;

public class TimeVaryingGraphExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Config config = Config.builder().withoutEncryption().build();

        try (Driver driver = GraphDatabase.driver("bolt://localhost:7687", AuthTokens.basic("username", "password"), config)) {
            try (Session session = driver.session()) {

                // Set up schema
                setSchema(session);

                // Add data
                LocalDateTime time1 = LocalDateTime.now();
                addFriendship(session, "Alice", "Bob", time1);
                LocalDateTime time2 = LocalDateTime.now().plusDays(1);
                addFriendship(session, "Alice", "Charlie", time2);

                // Query time-varying graph
                LocalDateTime queryTime = LocalDateTime.now().plusHours(12);
                System.out.println(getFriendships(session, queryTime));

            }
        }
    }

    private static void setSchema(Session session) {
        String schema = "CALL db.createLabel($label) YIELD label "
                      + "RETURN label";
        session.run(schema, Params.parameters("label", "Person"));
    }

    private static void addFriendship(Session session, String person1, String person2, LocalDateTime time) {
        String createPerson1 = "MERGE (p:Person {name: $name})";
        session.run(createPerson1, Params.parameters("name", person1));
        session.run(createPerson1, Params.parameters("name", person2));

        String createRelationship = "MATCH (a:Person {name: $name1}), (b:Person {name: $name2}) "
                                  + "MERGE (a)-[r:FRIENDS {time: $time}]->(b) ";
        session.run(createRelationship,
                    Params.parameters("name1", person1, "name2", person2, "time", time.toString()));
    }

    private static Result getFriendships(Session session, LocalDateTime time) {
        String query = "MATCH (a:Person)-[r:FRIENDS]->(b:Person) "
                     + "WHERE r.time <= $time "
                     + "RETURN a.name AS person1, b.name AS person2, r.time";
        return session.run(query, Params.parameters("time", time.toString()));
    }
}
```

In this example, we create nodes with the label "Person" and add a "FRIENDS" relationship with a "time" property. We query the friendships at a given time by filtering on this property. You can customize the schema, node labels, relationship types and properties based on your application requirements. For sharding, this example assumes a single Neo4j instance. You can connect to multiple Neo4j instances, partition the data based on a sharding key, distribute the processing, and aggregate the results.

