To create a multi-dimensional array in Java that can store and add more values to itself, follow these steps:

1. Declare a variable to represent the multi-dimensional array. For example:

```java
int[][] multiArray;
```

2. Initialize the multi-dimensional array with the desired dimensions. For example:

```java
multiArray = new int[3][4];
```

This creates a multi-dimensional array with 3 rows and 4 columns.

3. Add values to the multi-dimensional array using nested for loops. For example:

```java
for (int i = 0; i < multiArray.length; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < multiArray[i].length; j++) {
        multiArray[i][j] = i + j;
    }
}
```

This loop sets the value of each element in the multi-dimensional array to the sum of its row and column indices.

4. To add more values to the multi-dimensional array, use the same nested for loops but change the values being assigned. For example:

```java
for (int i = 0; i < multiArray.length; i++) {
    for (int j = 0; j < multiArray[i].length; j++) {
        multiArray[i][j] += i*j;
    }
}
```

This loop adds the product of the row and column indices to the existing values in each element of the multi-dimensional array.

