For example,

```java
public class ArrayClass {
    public int[] array = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};
}

```

Then, in the class where you want to access the array, you create an instance of the ArrayClass and use dot notation to access the array field or use the getter method.

For example,

```java
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayClass arrayClass = new ArrayClass();
        int[] myArray = arrayClass.array;
        // Alternatively, you can use a getter method
