To read a QR code using a Rust script and a webcam, you'll need the `image` crate for image processing, the `qrcode` crate for generating QR codes, the `rscam` crate for webcam access, and the `rust-qr-reader` crate for decoding QR codes.

Add the following to the `Cargo.toml` file:
```toml
[dependencies]
image = "0.23.14"
qrcode = "0.12.0"
rscam = "0.5.0"
rust-qr-reader = "0.1.0"
```

Now, you can create a Rust script called `qr_reader.rs` to access the webcam, capture an image, and read a QR code:

```rust
use image::{Rgb, RgbImage};
use rscam::{Capture, Config};
use rust_qr_reader::qr_from_image;

fn main() {
    // Set up the webcam.
    let camera_path = "/dev/video0"; // This is the camera path on Linux, adjust for your OS.
    let mut config = Config::default();
    config.interval = (1, 30); // 30 FPS.
    config.resolution = (640, 480);

    let mut camera = Capture::new(camera_path).expect("Failed to open camera");
    camera.start(&config).expect("Failed to start camera");

    // Wait for the stream to initialize.
    std::thread::sleep(std::time::Duration::from_secs(1));

    // Capture an image from the webcam.
    let frame = camera.capture().expect("Failed to capture frame");
    let width = frame.resolution().0 as u32;
    let height = frame.resolution().1 as u32;

    // Convert the frame to an RGB image.
    let image = RgbImage::from_raw(width, height, frame.into_raw()).expect("Failed to convert frame");

    // Attempt to read the QR code from the image.
    match qr_from_image(&image) {
        Ok(data) => {
            println!("QR code data: {:?}", data);
        },
        Err(e) => {
            eprintln!("Failed to read QR code: {:?}", e);
        },
    }
}
```

To compile and run the script, execute the following command in the terminal:

```bash
$ cargo build --bin qr_reader && cargo run --bin qr_reader
```

Make sure that the QR code is visible to your webcam. Once the script captures the QR code, it will print the encoded data in the terminal. Note that this script only captures one frame and attempts to read the QR code in that frame. You can modify the script to capture and process frames in a loop for continuous QR code scanning.

