It seems the error originates from the wrong date string formatting for the Moment.js library. To fix the error, you can do a simple check and parse the date string conditionally based on its input format.

Here's the modified version of the `uploadArchivedPaymentsHelper` function:

```javascript
import { doc } from 'firebase/firestore';
import moment from 'moment';

export const uploadArchivedPaymentsHelper = async (payments, profile_id) => {
  const collectionRef = "profile_billing";
  const profileDocRef = doc(FirebaseDB, "profile", profile_id);

  const parseDate = (dateStr, format) => {
    // Correct any possible '-' to '/'
    const normalizedDateStr = dateStr.replace(/-/g, '/');
    return moment(normalizedDateStr, format).toDate();
  };

  const uploadPayments = await Promise.all(payments.map(async (item, index) => {
    const payment = {
      tuscania_id: item.idClient,
      alias: item.houseNumber,
      concept: item.concept,
      type: item.service,
      invoice_date: parseDate(item.date_invoice, "MM/DD/YYYY"),
      billingNumber: item.billingNumber,
      amount: Number(parseFloat(item.amount).toFixed(2)),
      invoice_total: Number(parseFloat(item.total).toFixed(2)),
      payment_date: parseDate(item.date_payment, "MM/DD/YYYY"),
      payment_total: Number(parseFloat(item.amount_payment).toFixed(2)),
      status: "Pagada",
      profile: profileDocRef,
      residentialID: "Yd5MV7jkA0MjQeCmzKrZ",
    };

    const createPayment = await onCreateOrUpdate(collectionRef, payment);
  }));

  return uploadPayments;
};
```

The changes I made include:

1. Importing Moment.js and Firestore functions at the beginning.
2. Defining a `parseDate` function to process the date strings. It first replaces any '-' with '/', making sure dates are formatted with '/' as a separator. Then it uses Moment.js to convert the date string to a Date object.
3. Replacing `map` with `Promise.all` to correctly handle the asynchronous operations. This way, `uploadPayments` will be resolved when all the payment uploading operations have completed.

Now you can use this function to upload archived payments, and it should not throw the Invalid time value error.

