This solution uses a regular expression to match all substrings that are up to 500 characters long (including any whitespace), but it only includes whitespace in the chunk if that whitespace character appears within the 500 character limit. This way, it ensures that no word is split in half. The resulting chunks are stored in the `chunks` array. 

