To test the collision between two Oriented Bounding Boxes (OBBs) using `AABBVsAABB`, we can use two steps. First, we transform one OBB into the local space of the other OBB, reducing the problem to an AABB vs OBB test. Next, we perform the AABB vs AABB test in the local space, using a rotation matrix to check for intersections. Finally, we would need to transform any resulting collision points and normals back into the global space.

Here is a complete implementation of the `OBBVsOBB` function:

```cpp
std::optional<isect_s> OBBVsOBB(const vec2f& origin1, const vec2f& vMins1, const vec2f& vMaxs1, real32_t ang1, const vec2f& origin2, const vec2f& vMins2, const vec2f& vMaxs2, real32_t ang2) {
    // Calculate the transformation matrix and its inverse
    mat2f rot1 = mat2f(ang1);
    mat2f rot2 = mat2f(ang2);
    mat2f rotation = rot1 * rot2.transposed(); // Rotation from box2 space to box1 space
    mat2f inv_rotation = rotation.transposed(); // Inverse rotation, from box1 space to box2 space

    // Transform box2 (OBB) into box1 (AABB) local space
    vec2f local_origin2 = rot1 * (origin2 - origin1);

    // Compute the box2 (OBB) vertices in local space
    vec2f box2_verts[4] = {
        origin2 + rot2 * vec2f(vMins2.x, vMins2.y),
        origin2 + rot2 * vec2f(vMins2.x, vMaxs2.y),
        origin2 + rot2 * vec2f(vMaxs2.x, vMins2.y),
        origin2 + rot2 * vec2f(vMaxs2.x, vMaxs2.y)
    };

    // Compute the box2 (OBB) extents along each axis in local space
    vec2f local_vMins2 = rotation * box2_verts[0];
    vec2f local_vMaxs2 = local_vMins2;

    for (int i = 1; i < 4; ++i) {
        vec2f local_vert = rotation * (box2_verts[i] - origin1);
        local_vMins2 = vec2f::min(local_vMins2, local_vert);
        local_vMaxs2 = vec2f::max(local_vMaxs2, local_vert);
    }

    // Perform the AABB vs AABB test in local space
    std::optional<isect_s> local_result = AABBVsAABB(origin1, vMins1, vMaxs1, local_origin2, local_vMins2, local_vMaxs2);

    // If there's no intersection, return nullopt
    if (!local_result)
        return std::nullopt;

    // Transform the result collision normal and points back into the global space
    isect_s global_result = local_result.value();
    global_result.normal = inv_rotation * global_result.normal;

    if (global_result.points) {
        for (auto& point : global_result.points.value()) {
            point = origin1 + inv_rotation * point;
        }
    }

    return global_result;
}
```

This `OBBVsOBB` function handles the intersection calculation between two OBBs by first transforming one OBB into the local space of the other OBB, and then performing an AABB vs AABB test in the local space using the `AABBVsAABB` function. Finally, it transforms the resulting collision normal and points back into the global space before returning the intersection information.

